WEBVTT

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.020
<i>A series of events that started with the MacGuffin...</i>

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:11.490
<i>Everything that happened after
I met Souma Sumire two years ago...</i>

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:15.050
<i>Think, think, think.</i>

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.200
<i>The current ability rampage case...</i>

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.620
<i>That's part of Urachi Masamune's plan.</i>

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.990
<i>His goal is to force the Bureau
to play their trump card.</i>

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.380
<i>To get rid of all abilities in Sakurada.</i>

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.480
<i>What will he do next, then?</i>

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.880
<i>What does he need to do
for his plan to proceed smoothly?</i>

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.080
I don't mind you eating while I talk.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.900
I will, thank you.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.030
I wouldn't want the ice cream to melt.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.810
I'd like you to do something for me.

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:33.390
I generally take any job if it's from the Bureau.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:36.130
It's not a request from the Bureau, though.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.350
It's something personal.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:40.510
Personal? From you?

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.680
I'd like you to use your ability for me.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.190
What would I do?

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.090
Doesn't matter.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.950
Something big, but not too big.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:55.150
Then I'd like you to tell the Bureau
that you used your ability subconsciously.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.780
It's not possible to lie to the Bureau.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.950
I'll take care of that.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.110
I'm sorry, but I can't do that.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.160
Why?

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.900
I don't know what you're planning,
and I don't want to lie.

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:10.920
Yesterday, two ability rampage cases took place.

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.480
Rampage?

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.750
It's very dangerous.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.530
I'm really scared.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:19.090
I believe you witnessed one of those cases.

00:03:19.090 --> 00:03:20.720
Me?

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.810
You mean what happened in the supermarket?

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:23.700
That's right.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:27.000
I'd never laughed so much in my life.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.600
It didn't seem dangerous.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.560
The other one was a traffic accident, though.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.260
One of the drivers had some bad chest trauma.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:38.220
Fortunately, he made it through with some cracked ribs,

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:40.400
but someone could've easily died.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.740
And how is that related to your request?

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.240
The Bureau is currently shaken.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:49.570
They have to make an important decision,

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:51.000
but they currently can't.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:51.870
And that is?

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:57.480
This morning, a team that's supposed to deal
with the ability rampage cases had a meeting.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:03.080
They decided that if a particularly
dangerous ability goes berserk,

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.390
they'll use their last resort.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.160
If you say that you couldn't control your ability,

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:13.350
the Bureau will get rid of all abilities in Sakurada.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.470
Let me think for a bit.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:21.050
I'm not sure if getting rid of abilities is the
right thing to do, so I can't make a decision yet.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.260
I understand that.

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:24.820
But there's not much time left.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:25.700
Why?

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:29.880
Since multiple people's abilities have
gone berserk for no apparent reason,

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:32.200
it's only natural to restrain dangerous abilities.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:33.290
Restrain?

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.790
We make people unable to use their abilities.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.960
The Bureau is currently going around
town sealing dangerous abilities.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.800
Which means I'll also lose my ability soon.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.140
Actually, your ability is one
that should be sealed immediately.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:51.060
No matter how much we try to delay it,

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.850
the Bureau people will surely
appear within a few hours.

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:58.480
Why do you think all abilities should disappear?

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:01.510
I'm scared of abilities.

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:04.010
I've always been scared of them.

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:05.780
Even though you work for the Bureau?

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:08.690
I started working there exactly because I'm scared.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:12.370
I didn't want to avert my eyes from
something I know nothing about and fear.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.410
Are you still afraid?

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.810
Of course.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:19.460
I'm the advisor of the Service Club.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:23.430
It's the club Asai Kei and Haruki Misora are in.

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:24.610
And?

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:28.390
Those two take too much
unnecessary weight on their shoulders.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:32.060
Their abilities make them do that.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:35.780
He can't stand being able to
do something and not doing it.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.440
Even though there's no need to,
he ends up doing everything he can.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.610
You <i>should</i> do everything you can, though.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:45.930
Let's say you can save the world
by sacrificing your own life.

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:48.520
There's no need for you to die.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:51.880
Just because you happen to have an ability like that

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.500
doesn't mean that you should throw
your life away like some hero, that's cruel.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:58.390
Sakurada's abilities are over the top.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:01.320
Powers that defy laws of nature
and let you do anything

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:03.500
are way more than humans can handle.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.420
Putting your hope into such things,

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:09.760
and continuing to suffer because
you won't give up, is just too sad.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:13.860
Even without abilities, people can be happy.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:17.980
Will Ukawa Sasane help us?

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.100
She's trying to save the world,

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.820
which means that of course
she's on the side of the weak.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:26.730
There's no way she could ignore
what someone without an ability says.

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:29.320
Is that why you used Tsushima Shintarou?

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.970
He's pretty bright.

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.820
He doesn't hesitate to tell convenient lies,

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:38.030
and he agrees with my plan with all his heart.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:41.330
Is the restriction of abilities progressing?

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.130
Without problems, yes.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:46.210
We still can't find the person
working with Asai Kei, though.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.440
I see. That's fine.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.780
Everything is progressing according to plan.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:54.220
We'll probably be able to finish everything today.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.340
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.810
You're five minutes early.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:05.690
I'd like you to search for
a person called Ukawa Sasane.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:09.700
It feels like my ability's lately been
reduced to mere people-finding.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:12.530
Agasadai

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.010
Whatever.
Agasadai

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:15.030
Let's go.
Agasadai

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:27.220
Good morning, Nonoh.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:30.970
Morning.

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:33.470
I didn't expect to see you here today.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.980
And yet you still came?

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:36.850
Yes.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.400
Is it something related to Asai?

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.460
No. I just wanted to kill some time.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:43.170
I see.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:46.440
I'm here because I got a request from Asai.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.940
"If you spot Ukawa, please tell me."

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:54.370
"There's a chance she might be a small child,"

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:58.090
"so tell me if you find a girl
that looks like her as well."

00:07:58.090 --> 00:07:59.160
"Thank you."

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:03.640
What could it mean that she might be a small child?

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:05.690
Who knows... That's certainly strange.

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:07.040
Have you found her?

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:09.080
Just now, yeah.

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:14.640
Once you leave the shopping district,
there should be a small café.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:18.100
In front of it, there's a black car parked,

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.600
with Ukawa Sasane inside.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.080
Thank you.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.490
Ukawa's been found.

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:26.770
I'm sorry, but I'm going to run there.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.030
Where was she?

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.170
Close.

00:08:29.170 --> 00:08:30.820
About ten minutes if I run.

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:34.450
You didn't want to tell him anything?

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:35.630
No.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.580
Yes...

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:40.700
Which one is it?

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:44.770
I wanted to tell him something,
but didn't have any words to say.

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:45.960
What? I don't get it.

00:08:46.370 --> 00:08:48.940
Something big happened two days ago.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:50.650
What was it?

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:54.340
It was like happiness of all kinds
came to me in one big bundle.

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:57.360
Oh. So it wasn't anything bad.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:59.100
The exact opposite.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:00.720
Haruki...

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:04.480
Even if we didn't have our abilities,
I'd still want to spend time with you.

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:09.250
So, Haruki, I hope we'll spend
plenty of time together.

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:13.740
I'm truly happy.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.010
That's good.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.480
But there's still something I'm not happy about.

00:09:18.480 --> 00:09:21.360
I met Kei this morning just for a bit.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.060
I see.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:24.430
When I parted with him,

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:27.170
I told him "I'll be waiting for you".

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.240
And?

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.380
And that's all.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:32.630
I don't understand where the problem is.

00:09:32.910 --> 00:09:37.110
I didn't say "goodbye", not even "see you again",

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.790
but "I'll be waiting for you".

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:42.500
It was as if I was claiming my right to him,

00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:46.330
as if I wanted to tell him that I find
it obvious he'd come back to me.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:48.310
I chose those words knowing that.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.440
I've been so selfish recently.

00:09:52.850 --> 00:09:55.550
I still don't really understand the problem.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:58.570
Are you unhappy with yourself being selfish?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.160
I...

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:02.950
I want to stay selfish.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.700
Then there shouldn't be any problem.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:09.710
But I don't want to cause
Kei problems by being selfish.

00:10:09.710 --> 00:10:12.050
I see. That's complicated.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:16.470
But I'm sure that you won't cause
him problems by being selfish.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.600
I hope so.

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:23.170
But the truly selfish thing
about me lies somewhere else.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.770
When I met Kei this morning, he was tired.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.090
I'm sure he was very tired.

00:10:29.090 --> 00:10:31.610
I actually wanted to stay with him.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:37.360
I think I want to be able to naturally stay by his side.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.030
And to be able to help him at any time,

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:42.320
I want to become much more useful.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:47.550
I don't think it matters if you're
useful or not to stay near someone.

00:10:47.550 --> 00:10:50.500
If you want to improve, though, I think you should.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:02.850
<i>There, I guess.</i>

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.880
<i>I can't let Ukawa focus!</i>

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:46.260
Did you know this would happen?

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.970
I did.

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:49.310
Why didn't you prevent it?

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:52.600
To show you, of course.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.770
A young man pitied the roadside
trees whose branches were cut.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.280
That was what caused this.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:12:01.280
Do you think he used his ability on purpose?

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:03.660
Even if he was conscious of what he was doing,

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:07.410
it doesn't change the problem
happening in this town.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:08.540
Ukawa.

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.790
You're free to judge what is right or wrong.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.670
I understand.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.750
It is indeed dangerous.

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:21.050
Let's eliminate abilities from Sakurada.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.930
Mr. Tsushima! Why?

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:30.720
<b>PLEASE DON'T LEAVE BICYCLES OR MOTORBIKES HERE</b>

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.350
<i>Did I make it in time?</i>

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:56.880
You were late.

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.130
Please tell me,

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:02.300
is it wrong to drive if you're
going somewhere far away?

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:04.630
No, you can drive as much as you want.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.970
Is it against some rule to use a mobile phone

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.390
to talk to your loved ones at any time?

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.020
You can use it as much as you want.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.560
Is it wrong to be liked because you're pretty?

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.600
Is it wrong to live in luxury if you
were born to a wealthy family?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:18.940
What's wrong with any of that?

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.900
There's nothing wrong about it.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:21.650
So...

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:22.190
<b>PLEASE DON'T LEAVE BICYCLES OR MOTORBIKES HERE</b>

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:25.740
Why are only the abilities in Sakurada a problem?

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.620
Because I feel like they're unfair.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:33.000
And that's enough to disapprove of something.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.750
Kei.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.460
Become an ordinary high schooler.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:40.880
Focus on simple worries
like your future, dreams, love.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:45.010
And one day, give those up and
live a peaceful, happy life as an adult.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.970
That's exactly what I don't want.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:49.090
Children are always selfish like that.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:53.140
And adults are always under the impression
that whatever they think is common sense.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:54.850
Of course.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:57.390
Life is full of false impressions.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.950
Such nice weather.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:12.200
Look, when the sky is clear,
even small puddles look beautiful.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:15.450
Ukawa Sasane used her ability, didn't she?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.670
Yeah, and in a wonderful way.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.920
It was beautiful and blessed and
very problematic for the Bureau.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:27.670
The most dangerous ability user used her ability.

00:14:27.670 --> 00:14:29.550
It wasn't controlled.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:30.840
This will be the end.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.970
Are we doing the right thing?

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.970
Where do you see anything wrong?

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:40.980
I'm just pointing out a problem
that this town had from the start.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:43.730
The Bureau will now finally face this problem,

00:14:43.730 --> 00:14:45.650
and make the right decision.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:48.610
I hate this town.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:51.320
But I like the name.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.490
This town's name?

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.330
"Sakurada."

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:58.210
It's similar to a Spanish word that means "holy".

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.460
Sagrada Familia?

00:15:00.460 --> 00:15:03.170
That's "holy family".

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:05.250
It's Catalan, I think.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:08.920
I'll right the holy town.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.010
I'll rearrange it, removing the corrupted parts.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:14.600
Don't you agree it's a beautiful thing to do?

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.850
That's all I wish for.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.690
I want to like this town.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.730
Good job, Kei.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:27.780
Here's the last request.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.990
Can I borrow your shower?

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:38.120
According to my clairvoyance, I'm apparently
supposed to take a shower in your apartment.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.330
This will be the end.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:45.130
I'll tell you everything I know, just like I promised.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:48.590
I'll also make a really good
chicken curry while I'm at it.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:50.260
We'll eat it together.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:56.560
Hi, Asai! It's been a while.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.770
Hello.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.730
I have two matters to talk about.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:03.480
One is related to my job at the Bureau.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.150
The other is something personal.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:06.900
Which one should I start with?

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:08.190
Doesn't matter.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:11.200
Let's take care of my job quickly, then.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:16.200
As a member of the Bureau,
I have to confiscate one of your belongings.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.160
Do you know what it might be?

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:19.830
No, not really.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.830
That's a lie.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.210
It's not good to lie.

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.580
I just wasn't sure.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.170
What do you think it is?

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:28.460
A picture, maybe?

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:29.590
Exactly.

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:32.010
It's about Sasano Hiroyuki's ability,

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:35.470
and being able to meet with
a future-seer for just ten minutes.

00:16:35.470 --> 00:16:36.850
Could you hand it over?

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.680
I can't.

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.680
I burned Souma Sumire's picture yesterday.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.940
He's telling the truth.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:46.810
So you didn't want to give her picture away.

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:50.400
What about the other Witch, then?

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:51.490
The other Witch?

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:52.990
The nameless system.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.530
The first Witch.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:57.620
Don't you have a picture of her as well?

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.450
Yes, I do.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.250
Give it to us, then.

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.210
I guess I don't have a choice.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.960
Do you have any other pictures
taken by Sasano Hiroyuki?

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.040
I don't.

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:11.710
I only have that one picture.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.760
Then once we collect it,

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:16.220
our job here will be done.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:19.300
Please wait, I'll bring it.

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:22.720
Wait. Before that, I want to take care
of my personal matter as well.

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:26.060
This is just pure curiosity, you know.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:29.690
How much did you understand
of what was happening?

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.320
I don't know anything.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.240
I've just been guessing.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.110
I'd love to hear your guesses.

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:37.990
You're the culprit.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:39.530
The culprit?

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:40.870
What culprit?

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:45.460
In the case of four ability rampages
in Sakurada, beginning yesterday.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.500
Those were simply accidents.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.040
There's no culprit or anything.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:53.210
If you cause an accident on purpose, you're a culprit.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:57.180
You created an environment in which
an accident would happen with your ability.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:58.840
Such an interesting story.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:17:59.720
Continue.

00:18:00.050 --> 00:18:04.020
Yesterday, this girl's ability went
out of control at an intersection.

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:07.480
I was there when it happened, and saw her.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:11.520
But the girl I saw was around ten years old.

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:14.570
In this picture, she's at least in middle school.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.610
You might be remembering wrong.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.990
Please, it's impossible for me
to remember something wrong.

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:23.580
The same happened with
the boy in the supermarket.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:27.410
I got a good score on my last test,
and you said you'd buy it then!

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:29.710
The test was last month!

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.670
Neither of them was wrong.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:37.510
But the boy was talking from the
perspective of one month before that.

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:39.760
When people are unaware of their abilities,

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:41.970
they naturally go out of control.

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:44.770
Even if you were right about all that,

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:47.560
how can you blame my ability?

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.440
Because I know what it does.

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:54.440
Thank you very much for fixing my keychain.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:56.940
I always felt bad about it.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:59.150
I didn't thank you back then.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:03.120
I told you to go home quickly.

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:07.830
You should've left this town just like I told you to.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.790
So you remember.

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.170
Of course.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:14.800
The nameless system phoned you,
which was enough

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:16.590
to become wary of you.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:21.090
Back then, I wasn't even aware
of the existence of abilities.

00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:24.760
I never thought much about your ability.

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:27.060
But now I understand.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.940
You can rewind the time of an object.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:33.560
You can recreate the past
of a keychain... or of a human.

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:36.110
Isn't that what your ability does?

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:40.110
It's true that I possess an ability like that.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:44.990
But you see, you can't draw the conclusion that
I'm the culprit just because I'm able to do that.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:46.830
That's true.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:47.830
Asai.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:51.500
Do you know how the Bureau
will deal with this case?

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.750
They'll erase all information
about abilities from Sakurada.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:57.420
Huh... How do you know that?

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:59.510
I read the written copy of the Script.

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.720
I'm aware of what happened during the first year.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:06.970
Anyone who crosses the border
will forget about abilities.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:09.850
That's a rule that two ability users created.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:13.690
And soon this town will become
just like the outside of the border.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:16.150
It'll be a place where no one is aware of abilities.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.280
With just one exception.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.820
You, Asai.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:25.490
In those forty years, you were the only exception.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:29.870
I'd been wondering if you'd
appear here with a knife.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.330
I don't need a knife to do this.

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:37.460
Should I rewind your time to before you were born?

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:39.590
That's impossible.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:44.300
The most you can rewind with your ability
is most likely around two or three years.

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:45.590
Maybe five, at most.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:47.970
What makes you think that?

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:52.310
There was only one exception
to the four ability rampage cases.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:56.690
Ukawa used her ability out of her
own free will, not by losing control.

00:20:56.690 --> 00:21:01.190
I heard it's about five years ago
that she acquired her ability.

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:04.450
You couldn't rewind her time that far back.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.660
I see.

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.700
What about the two or three years estimate?

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:10.490
The keychain you fixed for me

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.250
broke again some time ago.

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:15.500
It was repaired, but there was still a small crack,

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.210
and from there, it broke in exactly the same way.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.840
Considering when that crack appeared,

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:23.090
and when you repaired the keychain for me,

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:26.760
I realized you must have rewound
its time to less than three years back.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:29.050
You figured it all out nicely.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:31.970
My curiosity is satisfied.

00:21:32.850 --> 00:21:34.520
One more thing.

00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:35.350
What is it?

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:41.230
How can I turn you into an
ordinary person with no abilities?

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:43.530
If you don't want to use a knife,

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:47.610
even I can't think of any way
to rid me of my memories.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.030
Those words...

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:51.490
are not a lie.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:56.460
Next Episode

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.830
People become kinder to accept themselves.

00:21:58.830 --> 00:22:00.340
I'm sure I can't save you.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.460
It's time to wake up from your dream.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:03.000
Could I borrow your shower?

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:04.760
You haven't told me anything.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:05.670
Souma Sumire!

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:07.630
I can't help being the same as her.

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:09.970
You're such a fool.

00:22:16.390 --> 00:22:20.360
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:26.570
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:32.830
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:33.120 --> 00:22:42.420
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:46.880
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:46.880 --> 00:22:49.260
You get lost while searching for

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:53.140
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:56.060
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:56.060 --> 00:22:59.480
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:02.110
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:02.110 --> 00:23:05.150
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:05.730 --> 00:23:08.320
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:11.950
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:11.950 --> 00:23:14.450
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:14.450 --> 00:23:16.200
If it were so simple to just

00:23:16.200 --> 00:23:19.210
Lock your own heart

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:22.330
How lovely life would be

00:23:22.330 --> 00:23:27.590
But I believe you have the key

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:33.930
To let my soul be free
